From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6afe + drm/msm/dp: complete the DisplayPort DEVICE_START the DSP holds

Traced on the Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250, vendor ADSP firmware; ftrace +
kprobes on afe_apr_send_pkt, q6afe_callback, apr_callback,
qcom_glink_native_rx, msm_dp_audio_enable, 2026-10-15): the DSP executes
AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START for DISPLAY_PORT_RX but, in about 40 % of the
starts, does not deliver the response until the DP audio engine toggles;
the response then arrives 2.7 ms after the engine is switched off, with no
host traffic in between. q6afe waited 3 s, failed the prepare, and the
stream (or PipeWire's one-time card probe, which marks the whole profile
unsupported) was lost. Enabling the engine only after the start (without
the hw_params mapping of the DRM audio helper) makes every start time out.

Wait 150 ms for that start instead of 3 s and treat a held response as
started (the late response is stored by the callback), and have
msm_dp_audio_prepare(), which the codec runs right after the cpu DAI's
prepare, switch an already-enabled engine off and on so the DSP completes
the start before data flows.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c	2026-10-15 14:49:18.468472099 +0900
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c	2026-10-15 14:50:11.162748443 +0900
@@ -1046,6 +1046,25 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6afe_get_port_id);
 
+/*
+ * HOLODOR: the DSP executes DEVICE_START for the DisplayPort port at once
+ * but delivers its response only on the next transition of the DP audio
+ * engine (Retroid Pocket 5, ftrace + kprobes 2026-10-15: no response for
+ * seconds, then the ack 2.7 ms after the engine toggles; ~40 % of starts).
+ * Do not stall 3 s on it: wait briefly, the port is started either way, and
+ * msm_dp_audio_prepare() (the codec prepare that follows) toggles the engine
+ * to complete it. The late ack is stored by the callback harmlessly.
+ */
+#define DP_START_TIMEOUT_MS 150
+
+static unsigned int afe_cmd_timeout_ms(struct q6afe_port *port, uint32_t rsp_opcode)
+{
+	if (port && port->id == AFE_PORT_ID_DISPLAY_PORT_RX &&
+	    rsp_opcode == AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START)
+		return DP_START_TIMEOUT_MS;
+	return TIMEOUT_MS;
+}
+
 static int afe_apr_send_pkt(struct q6afe *afe, struct apr_pkt *pkt,
 			    struct q6afe_port *port, uint32_t rsp_opcode)
 {
@@ -1073,7 +1092,7 @@
 	}
 
 	ret = wait_event_timeout(*wait, (result->opcode == rsp_opcode),
-				 msecs_to_jiffies(TIMEOUT_MS));
+				 msecs_to_jiffies(afe_cmd_timeout_ms(port, rsp_opcode)));
 	if (!ret) {
 		ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else if (result->status > 0) {
